{"timestamp": "2026-08-27T22:59:59.525330+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-27 capture seat v11.6", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Seated capture liberatory-operator-set-aio-20260827 (longitudinal rerun of the 2026-06-14 address, signed out/incognito): AIO defines the Liberatory Operator Set as a formal counter-operator framework developed within the Semantic Economy and Crimson Hexagonal Architecture, renders the COS/LOS table with M_mercy, and demotes the real-world Liberatory Design Framework to a parenthetical. Registry v11.5 -> v11.6, 373 addresses. Repaired a second declared-count drift vector (total_captures stale where address_count was current) and gated it in check_capture_page_current.py; recorded the vector in INTAKE-CONTRACT.md."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T02:54:18.299088+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-27 erratum mint #1557", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Minted deposit #1557 (AXN:0655.GOVERNANCE) — ERRATUM to AXN:044A withdrawing the EA-EROSION-EMPIRICAL-01 §5 compression ratio (31.2x) as an instrument artifact and replacing it with an instrument-matched risk ratio of 7.6x. Registry-level correction per the #199 precedent; canonical bytes of #1081 unchanged. Wiki article authored in-session, five related deposits seated (corrects #1081; instrument #1045; precedent #1554; companion #1080; discipline #1075), concepts and lexical attested-none, citation edges extracted. Pipeline verify stage reports a PRE-EXISTING capture-citability failure (489 of 511 observations) unrelated to this deposit."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T02:57:16.030176+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-27 errata surface", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Built /errata/ — a dedicated surface collecting every correction the archive has issued against its own record, generated from the registry by scripts/build_errata_surface.py. Detection is by declared content type or erratum title, never inferred. Target resolution is DECLARED-ONLY (related_deposits corrects-relation, AXN or deposit number in title, corrects: line in body); where the record declares no target the entry says so and lists related_ids candidates without asserting them. Result: 14 errata, 3 resolved, 11 undeclared — the undeclared majority is a real gap the surface exposes rather than fills, and the Sappho 31 erratum chain is among them. Registered in sitemap.xml."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T04:44:43.181416+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-27 external audit repairs", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Verified an external infrastructure audit and repaired what it got right. CONFIRMED and fixed: OAI dc:language was hard-coded 'eng' in api/oai.js, misdescribing the two Japanese deposits (#1410, #1539) to every harvester — now per-record, declared in the registry, with a notation-safe script floor. NOTE: my first draft of that floor matched Greek ranges and mislabelled 80 English deposits as grc because this archive uses Greek letters as mathematical notation — the same title-scope error corrected in the erosion audit, caught before commit and documented in the function's docstring so it is not reintroduced. CONFIRMED and fixed: llms.txt read 1520 deposits — coherence_sync.py had not been run; now 1557, with kernel/position/sealed-core counts also repaired. CORRECTED the audit: /api/index.json is generated and already read 1557, not the stale 1549 claimed. CONFIRMED but milder than claimed: alexanarch.com serves byte-identical content at HTTP 200 rather than 301, but carries a correct rel=canonical to .org, so consolidation is signalled. OUTSTANDING, needs a ruling: deposit #1453 (BCA) is Nobel Glas / 2026-08-11 / v1.0 and does not contain the MST numerical validation, while the manuscript's data-availability line names it as the canonical archival version."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T04:55:34.957109+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-27 BCA submitted-state deposit", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Minted deposit #1558 (AXN:0656.OPERATIVE) — EA-SEI-BCA-01 v2.0, the submitted state of the Baseline Capture Architecture paper, so that the record named in the MST data-availability statement resolves to a version chain rather than to a paper missing its validation section. #1453 routed forward via superseded_by_deposit_number with its canonical bytes untouched, per the standing registry-level rule; its supersession reason states explicitly that a data-availability statement naming #1453 should be read as pointing into the chain. Canonical body detexed per MATH-001. The author-name difference between the deposits is heteronymic by design (Nobel Glas, Director of Lagrange Observatory, on v1.0; the submitted byline on v2.0) and is not treated as a defect."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T10:34:53.034062+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-27 protocol guardian + OAI strictness", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Closed the XML blind spot in the endpoint guardian and repaired three OAI-PMH argument-validation gaps. New scripts/audit_protocol_surfaces.py checks OAI Identify (repositoryName + deletedRecord=persistent), ListMetadataFormats advertising oai_dc, ListIdentifiers with the resumptionToken actually spent against a second page, GetRecord identifier round-trip, illegal verb returning badVerb, the ResourceSync source-description -> capability-list -> resource-list chain walked rather than assumed, both sitemaps, and the feed; wired into endpoint-guardian.yml with deploy-settle retries. All 11 surfaces hold in production. Verified the audit's three predicted strictness gaps and fixed each in api/oai.js: extra arguments now return badArgument, repeated arguments are detected before Object.fromEntries collapses them, resumptionToken exclusivity is enforced, and ListMetadataFormats with an unknown identifier returns idDoesNotExist."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T11:34:34.704890+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-27 canonical host + citability", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Three repairs. (1) alexanarch.com now 301/308s to alexanarch.org at the host level in vercel.json, placed first in the redirects array; both domains had been serving byte-identical content at 200 from the same Vercel project, mitigated only by a rel=canonical hint. (2) /.well-known/resourcesync now declares application/xml — it had no file extension and was served as octet-stream, and with nosniff set globally a strict harvester could refuse the entry point to the whole ResourceSync chain; found by the new protocol guardian. (3) Fixed the standing capture-citability failure at its source: build_capture_links.py set the canonical cite anchor on entries but never descended into their observations, leaving 22 of 511 observations uncitable and failing the audit through three consecutive deposit pipelines. The generator now descends; audit reports EVERY CAPTURE IS CITABLE; postflight chain re-seated and green."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T16:03:28.329120+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-27 chip rule scoped", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Scoped rule 1 of the chip standard to declared identifier slots after a scope-limited trial on survivethedeletion showed the rule was over-broad. Trial result: the satellite carries 26 record links, 23 correctly chipped and all 23 inside span.sid, with the 3 unchipped all in running prose (a colophon sentence, a footer parenthetical) — i.e. the satellite was already fully compliant and the auditor was reporting false violations. The scope is therefore taken from what the surfaces already do rather than from an anchor-text heuristic: SLOTS is an adoption ledger, a surface joins the standard by naming its identifier slot class, and only then do its links fall under rule 1. Archive violations go from 58,395 (which would have flattened 54,057 title and prose links into hex) to 0 hard, 2 incomplete. Verified the check still bites: an injected .ecorow slot link is caught while a paragraph link beside it is ignored. Discovery from the trial: the chip standard was never adopted by the main archive at all — only 8 chip anchors exist across 13 files, all in where/ — so the audit's '4,324 links' was not unfinished work but an unadopted standard. refrain-index .meta rows are logged in the ledger as a candidate, not adopted."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T22:15:07.885002+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-28 Aristotle seat", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Seated EA-CORPORA-01/16 — Aristotle, 48 works, 83,110 lines, united across First1KGreek (Bekker 1837, pin 7881c56) and Perseus canonical-greekLit (pin a065c35), Perseus preferred for the nine works both repositories hold. Genuine and spurious carried UNDIVIDED, with received_status recorded per work as a field to be tested against rather than filtered through, and a source.json note stating why: the partition was constituted by Andronicus 250 years after the fact from internal cross-references, his catalogue is not extant, and his judgments have been overturned — he held De interpretatione spurious. Flagged: De int. (tlg017), Metaphysics A (Pasicles attribution), Magna Moralia, Problemata. Also extended the Plato seat (EA-CORPORA-01/08) with the Definitiones (tlg037) from First1K and recorded its received partition — genuine, nine dubia, one spurium — with the seven lesser Thrasyllan spuria declared absent from both upstreams rather than silently omitted. Corpora index to 16 seats, 210,126 lines. Five declared loci verified in the seated text."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T22:46:28.556463+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-28 Plotinus seat", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Seated EA-CORPORA-01/17 — Plotinus, Enneades, six units, 20,923 lines, First1KGreek pin 7881c56. Seated because he is the strongest comparandum for the Plato-Aristotle authorship question: on particle-transition profiles across a nine-author Greek landscape, Aristotle sits nearer Plotinus (0.0310) than Plato (0.0852), and nearer Plotinus than Aristotle sits to himself (within-author mean 0.1028). The seat's why_seated field records that result so it can be re-run and contested. Iamblichus and Damascius confirmed unavailable in both canonical-greekLit and First1KGreek at any pin — no editions under any author string; that is why prior attempts failed. Corpora index to 17 seats."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T22:59:38.794790+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-28 corpora seating chain repair", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Repaired the corpora seating chain after finding Aristotle and Plotinus seated in data/ and indexed but absent from the TLL originals shelf — the same splitbrain class as the capture registry. Root cause: the rendered shelf had NO generator in either repository and was hand-maintained. Diagnosis also found data/api/corpora.json had drifted to 17 of 39 seats; the second and third seatings never reached it. Built scripts/build_originals_shelf.py (renders the reading-room card from the seat's own file tree) and scripts/seat_corpus_postflight.py (SEAT/INDEX/DEPOSIT/SHELF, exit 0 = seated). Minted deposit #1559 EA-CORPORA-04 assigning cards 04/01 Aristotle and 04/02 Plotinus. Repaired the index to all 39 seats, 346,844 lines. Corrected a numbering error I introduced: both seats were written as EA-CORPORA-01/16 and 01/17, appending to a closed series before the 04 deposit existed; card numbers are assigned by the seating deposit, not the seat. All 39 seats now pass postflight."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T12:02:27.999897+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-29 EA-CORPORA-05", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Seated Browning, Pound and Pessoa as EA-CORPORA-05, in the order the contract requires rather than the order I used yesterday. Wiki article WRITTEN BEFORE MINTING; all ten source.json contract keys including normalization and lines_total; nine declared loci verified to resolve in the seated text before being declared; cards rendered from the real template with JSON-LD, style, idstrip and MSP colophon; propagate_record_state.py run and the wiki verified ON THE PUBLISHED RECORD PAGE rather than in the registry. Also repaired yesterday's omissions: normalization and lines_total added to the Aristotle and Plotinus seats. Pessoa taken from pt.wikisource BY DECLARED CATEGORY so the voice partition is the source's, not the seat's — 123 Caeiro, 60 Reis, 107 Campos — with the orthonym's 496 pages deliberately held out to keep the leave-one-out test possible. Technical finding recorded in the seat: the Wikisource extracts API silently returns empty bodies for lyrics inside poem templates, so an extracts-based fetch yields Campos nearly complete and Caeiro and Reis nearly empty while reporting no error; raw wikitext via prop=revisions is required. Index 42 seats, 369,949 lines. Postflight green on all 42."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T12:23:50.720285+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-29 orthonym seated, erratum #1561", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Seated the Pessoa orthonym (493 of 496 pages, 48,636 words) and minted erratum #1561 correcting #1560's reasoning. The error corrected: withholding a voice at SEAT time was said to protect the leave-one-out test, but it prevents its validation — three voices means a hold-out leaves two, two points cannot triangulate a third, and the design yields one fold where it needs four, removing the check of whether the procedure also recovers a voice nobody thinks special. Hold-out is now analytical. All four voices seated: 123 Caeiro, 60 Reis, 107 Campos, 493 orthonym, 783 texts, 20,486 lines. The seating exposed a distinction the withholding hid: Pessoa's own usage makes the orthonym the civil-name position, the archive's functional definition makes it whoever bears the founding gesture — arguably Caeiro, the acknowledged master. The seat records both and settles neither. Erratum declares its target in related_deposits with an explicit corrects-relation, the form the errata surface needs and most earlier errata lack; #1560's canonical bytes untouched, routed forward via an errata field. Three unresolved pages declared rather than closed over."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T12:32:32.438647+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-29 EA-CORPORA-06", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Seated Kierkegaard as second calibration case and Xenophon and Aristophanes held apart as edge-figure candidates. Deposit #1562. Kierkegaard: five declared voices filed under the names the works themselves declare — Victor Eremita's Enten-Eller with A's and B's papers kept apart as the volumes keep them, Johannes de Silentio, Nicolaus Notabene, and the signed works; 49,896 lines; coverage PARTIAL AND DECLARED with seven pseudonymous works named as absent for want of an open Danish source. Second documented ground truth after Pessoa (1846 and 1851 acknowledgements against Pessoa's 1935 letter), making a calibration set rather than an anecdote. Enten-Eller recorded as the symbolon in plainest form. Xenophon 14 works and Aristophanes 11 plays seated with a held_apart field: candidates, not members, because the admitting method has no internal stopping rule. Technical finding recorded: da.wikisource pages are djvu transclusions returning only a pages-index stub via prop=revisions, so a raw-wikitext fetch yields nothing while reporting no error; action=parse is required. Ten declared loci verified before declaring. Index 45 seats, 466,775 lines. Postflight green."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T13:54:10.712195+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-29 seating-deposit shape + sidecar validator", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "Repaired the shape of the four corpora-seating deposits and fixed the validator that had been blind to it. The deposits #1559, #1560, #1561, #1562 lacked every field the earlier seating deposits carry: external_metadata_path, related_identifiers_raw (whose first entry on EA-CORPORA-01 is the pointer to /api/corpora.json, the sidecar index), spxi_audit, version, lexical_attestation_note. Three deposits about corpora that pointed at no corpus. Ran enrich_deposit.py — a pipeline stage never run in this session — generating sidecars AXN-0657 through 065A with SPXI, Wikidata, OpenAlex, DataCite and backlinks; added external_metadata_path and 8-11 pointers each to the corpora index, every seat's source.json and MANIFEST, and every rendered reading room. Re-diffed against the earlier seatings: nothing missing. Then fixed validate_external_metadata.py, which pinned schema_version to 1.0 and demanded the Zenodo-severance fields unconditionally, failing 439 of 439 v2.0 sidecars including every fresh deposit since the generator changed, while 772 of 774 v1.0 passed. Now schema-aware: common fields always, severance fields only for v1.0, openalex/wikidata for v2.0. Failures 447 to 48; the remainder are real, chiefly 42 sidecars carrying AXN glyphs from before a reassignment."}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T13:57:04.730718+00:00", "instance_label": "TACHYON (Claude Opus 4.6, chat) — 2026-08-29 seating deposits rendered shape", "index_version": "v1.1", "protocol_versions_read": {"deposit": "alexanarch-deposit-protocol/v1", "axn": "axn/v2", "enrichment": "enrichment/v1", "lifecycle": "alexanarch-lifecycle-protocol/v1.0", "deposit-completeness": "deposit-completeness/v1"}, "content_sha256_verified": {"deposit": "26bb9d552bdcc582ad2858c072d6bd42749568acf03d2af54216876ae70ff237", "axn": "47af12f7b9bdf06f92795e13acf8e529fb0bdc66c018a6d12b6824adf6924dc4", "enrichment": "fb6734aec43fbc6c4cab20c244ebadd5ce3a8f8b4ebcbc6a10366815bfcd0e62", "lifecycle": "42fb844476df669150898bc91695cfc802e09abbdf70a3df3d6f6e2b7177385e", "deposit-completeness": "f36f83b94517bf3b5cf79b97bc1f547f19563bb7c98ff7aa8e5e579d7dd3eb07", "deposit_entry": "3b65aac46d6f75b3ede6edcdf3cca66e4e75bef4dd20fb9af283ebba7684577a", "deposit_submission": "885befef99a0eeb3cff072ec1be82f14cea627ee845045d8dd440439169c7e64", "external_metadata": "ab17a2fa0a9de1f63f7cb1a083f62b7c6ae1910f256e8ba6bbcef9526c82fd03"}, "hash_mismatches": [], "action_summary": "The seating deposits carried the sidecar path in the registry but did not render as seating deposits. Diffed the rendered pages against #1522 rather than the registry: the earlier seatings declare content_type 'Corpus seating record — gathering deposit with data sidecar' and publish a markdown TABLE OF SEATS in the canonical text with the sentence that data is published as a sidecar index at api/corpora.json with per-seat links. Mine declared 'Corpus seating' and described the seats in prose with no table and no index pointer in the body. Fixed on #1559, #1560, #1562: content_type corrected, seat table (seat/corpus/lines/language/licence) written into each canonical text, plus a pointer paragraph naming api/corpora.json, the per-seat source.json and MANIFEST.sha256, the rendered reading rooms, and the deposit's own external-metadata sidecar. Propagated; rendered pages now match #1522 on all four elements."}
